# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF line endings on every
# system. The program embeds some of them (presets, templates, page assets)
# and the tests compare others byte for byte, so Git for Windows must not turn
# them into CRLF. Fixtures keep their exact bytes, CRLF cases included,
# through their own rule in fixtures/.gitattributes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Expected-output files are compared byte for byte by the tests: no
# conversion at all.
*.expected.txt -text
